{"availability":"available","full":"vortex378/workforceos","name":"workforceos","description":"Timesheets and approvals with PostgreSQL, transactional decisions, audit history, tests and a live demo","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-18T22:22:19Z","updated":"2026-09-18T22:26:07Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://workforceos-sigma.vercel.app","topics":["nextjs","postgresql","timesheets","typescript","vercel","workflow"],"demo":"https://workforceos-sigma.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:02.529Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:02.529Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:02.529Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:02:02.529Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A working timesheet and approvals product, built as a full-stack engineering case study.","WorkforceOS models a small but real operational workflow: employees record time, submit it, and a manager approves or rejects it. The dashboard, queue, and audit log all read from PostgreSQL. Each visitor receives a private demo workspace with synthetic data, so the public demo is safe to explore.","The interesting part of a timesheet system is not the form. It is the consistency of decisions under multiple actors and repeated requests. This repository focuses on the workflow boundary:"],"features":["Role checks on the server: team members can submit only their own entries; only the manager can decide a submitted entry.","Explicit state machine: draft → submitted → approved/rejected, with resubmission after rejection. Invalid transitions fail.","Transactional decisions: SELECT ... FOR UPDATE locks the entry while the status and audit event are written in one transaction. Duplicate decisions cannot both succeed.","Database constraints: valid statuses, hour bounds, and one entry per person, project, and date within a demo workspace.","Private visitor data: an opaque, HTTP-only cookie points to a dedicated workspace. Sample records are fictional."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vortex378/workforceos/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"2cb9c10955f8df6e5c354ecdfe874dfc0a0ed5792ee75fae6dab19e07f11261e","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:02.619Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:02.619Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A working timesheet and approvals product, built as a full-stack engineering case study.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vortex378/workforceos/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"The role checks demonstrate the domain boundary inside one isolated sandbox; a production tenant would add real sign-in, organization membership, authorization middleware, rate limiting, retention policy, and operational monitoring.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vortex378/workforceos/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"2cb9c10955f8df6e5c354ecdfe874dfc0a0ed5792ee75fae6dab19e07f11261e","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vortex378/workforceos/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:02.619Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-18T22:26:07Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vortex378/workforceos/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:02.619Z","hash":"2cb9c10955f8df6e5c354ecdfe874dfc0a0ed5792ee75fae6dab19e07f11261e","originalBytes":4930,"storedBytes":4930,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["demo","npm","run","audit","entry","manager","submitted","workflow","decisions","api","checks","private","src","state","submit","workspace","app","creates","creation","data","database","draft","one","postgresql","production","project","real","rejected","role","sandbox","visitor","approval","approved","approves","authentication","bash","blocked","both","boundary","build","built","cannot","case","check","constraints","dashboard","date","duplicate","each","entries","event","http","invalid","lib","lint","live"